<%# The report written out: the three figures in the row are a glance — a cost, a
    cache share, a slice of the context window — and this is the same report
    spelled out. How the tokens split, which model answered, what the cache
    saved.

    The allowance used to sit at the bottom of this panel; it has a sheet of its
    own now (see `_quota_sheet`), because it is the one reading a reader comes
    back to and it should not be behind a scroll.

    It is a `<details>` rather than a dialog so it needs no script to open. The
    panel hangs above the status line instead of pushing it: the line is at the
    bottom edge of the screen, and a panel below it would open off the page.

    These facts are drawn with the page, then kept current by the same
    out-of-band swap that moves the row. -%>
<details class="usage-sheet usage-sheet-facts">
  <summary class="usage-toggle" title="Pemakaian" aria-label="Pemakaian">
    <%= usage_icon(:usage) %>
  </summary>

  <div class="usage-panel" role="group" aria-label="Pemakaian">
    <%= View.render("_usage_facts", **facts) %>

    <%# The door out of the pinned prompt. It sits behind a panel rather than in
        the row because it is not a reading: it is something a reader does once
        in a while, and it costs one request without a cache. The note says so
        before the press, not after. -%>
    <p class="panel-title">Prompt</p>
    <div class="usage-repin">
      <button type="button" class="btn"
              hx-post="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/repin<%= h(token_query) %>"
              hx-target="#repin-note" hx-swap="innerHTML">Bangun ulang</button>
      <p class="usage-note" id="repin-note">Memory, skill, dan AGENTS.md yang berubah di tengah sesi baru masuk setelah compaction — atau di sini, dengan ongkos satu request tanpa cache.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
